11: Best Practices & Common Pitfalls
Instructor Cue: "Let me share the mistakes I've seen developers make over and over again with Angular authentication."
Pitfall 1: Storing Tokens Insecurely


❌ BAD:
// Don't do this
localStorage.setItem('token', token);  // Vulnerable to XSS


✅ BETTER:
// Use httpOnly cookies (set by backend)
// Or at minimum, use sessionStorage for short-lived tokens
Pitfall 2: Not Handling Token Expiration


❌ BAD:
// Token expires but UI doesn't know
// User clicks around, gets errors everywhere


✅ GOOD:
// Error interceptor catches 401 and auto-logs out
if (error.status === 401) {
   authService.logout();
   router.navigate(['/auth/login']);
}


Pitfall 3: Scattered Auth State


❌ BAD:
// Multiple components managing their own auth state
@Component({ ... })
export class HeaderComponent {
   isLoggedIn = localStorage.getItem('token') !== null;
}


@Component({ ... })
export class SidebarComponent {
   user = JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem('user') || 'null');
}


✅ GOOD:
// Single source of truth in AuthService
@Injectable({ ... })
export class AuthService {
   currentUser = signal<User | null>(...);
   isLoggedIn = computed(() => !!this.currentUser());
}


Pitfall 4: Not Using Guards


❌ BAD:
// Check auth in every component
ngOnInit() {
   if (!localStorage.getItem('token')) {
       this.router.navigate(['/login']);
   }
}


✅ GOOD:
// Use route guards
{
   path: 'dashboard',
   canActivate: [authGuard],
   component: DashboardComponent
}
Pitfall 5: Exposing Sensitive Data in Templates


❌ BAD:
<!-- Password visible in form state -->
<p>Your password: {{ password }}</p>


✅ GOOD:
<!-- Never expose sensitive data -->
<p>Welcome, {{ user().name }}</p>
Pitfall 6: Not Clearing State on Logout


❌ BAD:
logout() {
   localStorage.removeItem('token');
   // Forgot to clear user data!
   // Forgot to reset signals!
}


✅ GOOD:
logout() {
   this.currentUserSignal.set(null);
   this.tokenSignal.set(null);
   localStorage.removeItem('auth_token');
   localStorage.removeItem('current_user');
   this.router.navigate(['/auth/login']);
}
Best Practices Checklist
* Use Signals for auth state (not BehaviorSubject)
* Single source of truth in AuthService
* HTTP Interceptor for automatic token attachment
* Error Interceptor for 401 handling
* Route Guards for protected routes
* Lazy loading for better performance
* Reactive Forms for validation
* Built-in Control Flow for clean templates
* Standalone Components (no NgModules)
* Type safety with interfaces matching backend
* Environment configs for different stages
* Clear state on logout
* Handle loading states in UI
* Show error messages from backend
